2. Differences from the official builds

   - GOARCH=arm64. The official releases provide windows-386 and
     windows-amd64 only.
   - CGO_ENABLED=0. The Windows ICMP proxy (ingress/icmp_windows.go, which
     requires cgo) is therefore not compiled in; the generic fallback is
     used instead. The official windows-386 build is also built with
     CGO_ENABLED=0.
   - The built-in auto-update is disabled through the linker flag
     -X github.com/cloudflare/cloudflared/cmd/cloudflared/updater.BuiltForPackageManager=...
     because the updater would replace this executable with a build of a
     different architecture.
   - Build flags: -mod=readonly -trimpath -ldflags "-s -w" plus the version
     stamping flags (main.Version, main.BuildTime) used by the upstream
     Makefile.
   - The executable is not code-signed.

